  "nl_text": "The database schema named 'schemabench_0086' consists of five tables: 'subscriptions', 'users', 'subscription_items', 'receipts', and 'tax_rates'.\nThe 'subscriptions' table is used to store information about user subscriptions. It has columns for 'id', 'user_id', 'name', 'stripe_id', 'stripe_status', 'stripe_price', 'quantity', 'trial_ends_at', 'ends_at', 'updated_at', and 'created_at'. The 'user_id' column is a foreign key referencing the 'id' column in the 'users' table.\nThe 'users' table stores information about users. It has columns for 'id', 'stripe_id', 'pm_type', 'pm_last_four', 'pm_expiration', 'extra_billing_information', 'trial_ends_at', 'billing_address', 'billing_address_line_2', 'billing_city', 'billing_state', 'billing_postal_code', 'billing_country', 'vat_id', and 'receipt_emails'.\nThe 'subscription_items' table stores information about subscription items. It has columns for 'id', 'subscription_id', 'stripe_id', 'stripe_product', 'stripe_price', 'quantity', 'updated_at', and 'created_at'. The 'subscription_id' column is a foreign key referencing the 'id' column in the 'subscriptions' table.\nThe 'receipts' table stores information about user receipts. It has columns for 'id', 'user_id', 'provider_id', 'amount', 'tax', 'paid_at', 'updated_at', and 'created_at'. The 'user_id' column is a foreign key referencing the 'id' column in the 'users' table.\nFinally, the 'tax_rates' table stores information about tax rates. It has columns for 'id', 'stripe_id', 'percentage', 'updated_at', and 'created_at'. All columns allow null values except for 'id' and 'stripe_id', which do not allow null values. The 'stripe_id' column is unique.\nAll tables have primary keys, which are auto-incrementing and are used as unique identifiers for each record. The primary keys are 'id' in 'subscriptions', 'users', 'subscription_items', 'receipts', and 'tax_rates'. The 'user_id' and 'subscription_id' columns in the 'receipts' and 'subscription_items' tables reference the 'id' columns in the 'users' and 'subscriptions' tables respectively. The 'user_id' column in the 'receipts' table has an update and delete rule of CASCADE, meaning that if a record in the 'users' table is updated or deleted, the corresponding records in the 'receipts' table will also be updated or deleted.",
  "gold_question": "1) Background / Context\n\nThe project aims to develop a subscription billing solution built on Laravel, leveraging the Laravel Cashier package. This system targets SaaS businesses, facilitating subscription management through an integrated billing portal using Stripe and Paddle. The system simplifies recurring billing and customer invoice management, serving as a robust starting point for new SaaS applications.\n\n 2) Objectives\n\n- Develop a comprehensive subscription billing system for Laravel-based applications.\n- Enable easy management of subscription plans and customer billing.\n- Support multiple payment providers, including Stripe and Paddle, to handle transactions.\n- Provide a flexible billing experience for customers, including per-seat billing options.\n\n 3) Stakeholders & Users\n\n- SaaS Business Owners: Individuals or entities looking to implement subscription billing in their applications.\n- Customers: Users subscribing to SaaS services and managing their billing information via the portal.\n- Developers: Software engineers who will integrate and manage the billing system within their SaaS platforms.\n\n 4) Functional Descriptions\n\n- Subscription Management: Define and manage monthly or yearly subscription plans via a configuration file.\n- Customer Billing Portal: Provide a standalone portal where customers can subscribe to or modify plans, update payment methods, and download invoices.\n- Invoice Handling: Automatically generate and email PDF invoices to customers for each billing cycle.\n- Payment Provider Support: Integrate with Paddle to accept payments, including PayPal, enhancing payment flexibility.\n- Per-Seat Billing: Implement the capability to charge customers based on the number of team members or projects.\n- Frontend Flexibility: Maintain an isolated billing portal frontend, allowing the main application frontend to use any preferred technology stack.\n- System Upgrades: Ensure straightforward updates to the system without interfering with the core application code.\n\n 5) Non-Functional Descriptions\n\n- Scalability: Support an increasing number of customers and subscription transactions efficiently.\n- Security: Ensure secure handling of payment information and comply with relevant regulatory standards.\n- Usability: Provide an intuitive user interface in the billing portal for seamless interaction.\n- Extensibility: Allow future enhancements and integrations without significant rework of the existing system.",
  "input_json": "/data/SchemaBench/Experiment/schema2text_deepseek/0086.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0086\nCREATE TABLE `users` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `stripe_id` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `pm_type` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `pm_last_four` char(4) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `pm_expiration` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `extra_billing_information` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `trial_ends_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `billing_address` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `billing_address_line_2` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `billing_city` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `billing_state` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `billing_postal_code` varchar(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `billing_country` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `vat_id` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `receipt_emails` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `stripe_id` (`stripe_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `subscriptions` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `stripe_id` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `stripe_status` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `stripe_price` decimal(10,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `quantity` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `trial_ends_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `ends_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `subscriptions_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `subscription_items` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `subscription_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `stripe_id` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `stripe_product` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `stripe_price` decimal(10,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `quantity` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `subscription_items_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`subscription_id`) REFERENCES `subscriptions` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `receipts` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `provider_id` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `amount` decimal(10,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `tax` decimal(10,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `paid_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `receipts_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `tax_rates` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `stripe_id` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `percentage` decimal(5,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `stripe_id` (`stripe_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
